WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.890
- Hey, I'm dr Mike Varshavski,

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.000
a board certified family
medicine physician.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.108
And I wanna take on the top 10 questions

00:00:06.108 --> 00:00:09.740
on COVID-19 that I received
from my friends, family,

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.670
social media, and even my patients.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.120
Can pets transmit COVID-19?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.170
The answer to that question
is both yes and no.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.050
No, because pets don't seem to be having

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.380
symptoms of COVID-19,

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.290
they're not coughing,
they're not having fevers.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.380
So we're saying that they don't
seem to be infected with it.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.180
That being said, if you go for a walk

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.480
and you have a very cute puppy, like Bear,

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.940
and someone wants to pet it,

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.590
and they just sneezed into their hands,

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.740
and they touch your dog,

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.050
and now your dog comes
home, you touch your dog,

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.190
you could bring that virus

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.880
and introduce it into your own body.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.150
So yes, pets can be carriers
of this virus as a surface.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:44.900
So if you're gonna be
socially distancing yourself,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.630
also get your pets to socially
distance themselves too.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.920
Should I use soap to wash my produce?

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.350
Well, I've actually gotten
this question a lot recently

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.500
because of a viral video of
a doctor doing just that.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.840
And the truth of the matter is,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.420
not only do you not need
to do this, you shouldn't.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.440
Most fruits and vegetables are porous,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.200
meaning they can absorb the soap

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.740
and that's not great for your stomach.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.380
It can cause all sorts of
gastrointestinal symptoms

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.470
like nausea, vomiting, diarrhea.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.960
All you have to do to disinfect
your fruits and vegetables

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.660
is to run them under cold water.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.800
That's gonna get 90 to 95%

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.700
of whatever is out there off of them.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.370
Is it okay if I throw a mini party

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.930
but we all stay six feet apart?

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.900
The answer to this question is a hard no.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.400
Social distancing means
physical distancing,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.110
and more than six feet apart.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.110
The reason why we give
the six foot guidance

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.270
is in case you have to go out,
to do your grocery shopping,

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:37.130
or you're an essential employee
like a doctor or a nurse,

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.720
then yeah, six feet makes
sense to mitigate the risk.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.410
It's not 100% foolproof.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.170
Imagine one of your friends comes over,

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.720
they're asymptomatic, meaning
they're having no symptoms,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.159
but they have COVID-19,
now they give it to you,

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:50.580
you give it to one of your
family members in your home,

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.112
and they have serious consequences.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.640
Not something you want.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.970
Should I be taking an
immune boosting supplement?

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.760
I get really mad when I see claims

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.300
made by marketing companies

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.370
saying that they have an
immune boosting shake,

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.890
or detox drink, or supplement.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.960
They don't exist.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.400
There's no such thing as
boosting your immune system.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.750
Your immune system works

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.530
because you have vitamins,
minerals inside your body

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.500
that you get naturally from foods

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.530
or they're created within your own body.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.870
You do not need more of them.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:18.340
The analogy I like to give folks

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.790
is like a construction site.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.030
If you want to construction
to be done sooner,

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:23.770
you can't just deliver more materials

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.339
and think that's gonna
speed up the process.

00:02:25.339 --> 00:02:27.262
In fact, I can create more problems.

00:02:27.262 --> 00:02:31.171
So no, taking a huge amount
of vitamin D, and C, and E,

00:02:31.171 --> 00:02:34.240
and zinc is not gonna
help you protect yourself

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.560
from COVID-19, it's
just never been proven.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.710
Well, if not supplements, how
can I boost my immune system?

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:40.670
Well, the answer is, again,

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.190
you're not trying to
boost your immune system,

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:43.500
you're trying to optimize it.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.210
In fact, a boosted immune
system almost makes it sound

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.730
like you have an autoimmune disorder

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.980
where your own immune system
is attacking your body.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:50.813
You don't want that.

00:02:50.813 --> 00:02:52.020
To optimize your immune system,

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.071
you should focus on the
four pillars of health.

00:02:54.071 --> 00:02:56.920
Sleep, getting at least
seven to nine hours a night.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.123
Studies have shown that if
you get less than six hours,

00:02:59.123 --> 00:03:02.350
it drops her natural
killer cells by up to 50%

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:05.047
and they're responsible for
protecting you from COVID-19.

00:03:05.047 --> 00:03:08.150
Two, eat healthy, get
fruits, get vegetables,

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.940
make sure you're loading
up on the good stuff.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:14.240
Three, exercise now is no better
time than ever to exercise.

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:16.610
Do some sit-ups, take a class on your TV,

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:19.990
on your iPad, iPhone, or
go out for a run like I do.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.970
I've fallen in love with
running because of Nike.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.455
And four, don't engage in bad habits.

00:03:24.455 --> 00:03:26.520
Smoking can increase your chance

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.130
of having a severe case of
COVID-19, two to three times.

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:32.263
Overdrinking impairs your monocytes.

00:03:32.263 --> 00:03:33.590
It's a type of white blood cell

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.420
that protects you from COVID-19.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.970
Is COVID-19 an airborne virus?

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.330
The preliminary research says no.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.060
It looks like the main form
of transmission for this virus

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.760
is through respiratory droplets.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.610
That's what happens when
you sneeze or cough,

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.770
and you see that fine mist
shoot out into the air.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.490
Now those germ particles
tend to be heavier,

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.050
so they don't spend a
lot of time in the air,

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.720
they end up falling to the ground.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.110
Now these germs do have some hang time,

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.950
and I've seen media already
make a huge spectacle

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.712
that this virus can live in
the air for up to three hours.

00:04:02.712 --> 00:04:05.481
While yes, we've seen small particles,

00:04:05.481 --> 00:04:08.440
actually genetic material of this virus

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.180
live in the air for a
period of up to three hours.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.350
We have no evidence that those particles

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.880
can actually get people sick.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.680
So for now, the main forms of spread

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:17.950
we need to be concerned about

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.360
is respiratory droplets and contact.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.860
So you really have to avoid touching

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.720
your mouth, nose, or eyes

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.450
'cause that's how the
virus enters your system.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.810
As an exception for medical facilities,

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.220
when we're doing specific
procedures like an intubation,

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.880
or we have a patient on a specific type

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:34.860
of breathing machine called BIPAP,

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.200
we have seen some particles
of this virus aerosolized,

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.360
that's why the medical setting,

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.050
we have really quality protection

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.840
like N95 masks, or PAPA systems,

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.300
so the medical professionals
don't get sick around them.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.250
What can I do to lower my anxiety

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.200
and depressive symptoms during quarantine?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.520
The first issue that arises
during the quarantine

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.600
is a lack of social connections.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.530
We as humans are social beings,

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.410
we need that type of interaction.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.290
Remember, we're all in the same boat here.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.010
There's no FOMO to be had.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.633
So reach out and schedule
a date on FaceTime.

00:05:04.633 --> 00:05:06.960
Do a Skype with their entire family

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.680
so you could stir up a little trauma.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.350
Just keep that interaction in your life,

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.490
it's really important.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.870
Second, limit your time on the internet

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.110
and checking the news.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:17.750
My God, all the numbers
being thrown at you,

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.300
the outbreak warnings.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.920
This is really anxiety provoking.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.550
So check it once a day, or
maybe even every other day.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.240
And three, pick up a new hobby,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.510
painting, reading, exercising, anything,

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.500
because as someone wise once said,

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.970
an idle mind is a devil's playground.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:36.830
Is it true that taking
ibuprofen or Advil slash Motrin

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.030
can make COVID-19 symptoms worse?

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:40.770
This started when the French minister

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.700
came out and made a warning about this.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.680
There has been zero evidence

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:48.872
that shows ibuprofen directly
makes COVID-19 symptoms worse.

00:05:48.872 --> 00:05:51.470
The WHO even came out and
made a statement about this

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.180
saying that they did not advise

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.370
discontinuing ibuprofen
in COVID-19 patients.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.290
That being said, we're
still doing more research,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.550
and we're still figuring
out how it can play a role

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:03.570
in COVID-19 symptoms,
but the answer is easy,

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:05.200
if you don't have to take ibuprofen

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.470
and you have an other option

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:10.430
like acetaminophen, a.k.a
Tylenol, do it and ease your mind.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.390
Should the general public be wearing masks

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.330
to decrease spread of COVID-19?

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.770
There are two types of masks

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.560
that are being discussed
in this conversation.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.509
First, our N95 masks.

00:06:19.509 --> 00:06:21.920
These are the professional
form-fitting masks

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.320
you see doctors and nurses
wear on the front lines

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.850
to protect themselves.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:28.040
These masks keep the virus out.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.290
Then you have the loose-fitting,
inexpensive surgical masks

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.060
that actually prevent you
from putting the virus out.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.130
So basically this is
meant for sick people.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.400
If a patient comes into my office,

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.500
they're coughing all over the place,

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.230
we put one of these masks on.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.560
Now with COVID-19, having so many

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.270
asymptomatic sick patients,

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.100
meaning that we don't
even know they're sick,

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.340
perhaps there's some logic

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.320
in having everyone wear these masks.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.660
Well the WHO has never recommended

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.380
for the general healthy public,

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.830
to wear these surgical masks.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.480
First, there's a huge
shortage of these masks

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.200
right now for us as health professionals.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.080
Two, it gives you a
false sense of security

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:04.187
to feel like, "Oh maybe I can go out

00:07:04.187 --> 00:07:06.200
"cause I'll just wear
this inexpensive mask."

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.120
Remember, it doesn't protect
you, it protects everyone else.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.160
And then three, there's really
limited scientific research

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:14.490
saying that it truly
helps flatten the curve.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:16.620
Is ordering food delivery safe?

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.650
Nothing is 100% safe,

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.320
but if you're gonna be
ordering food delivery,

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.913
do it the best way you can
and take some precautions.

00:07:22.913 --> 00:07:25.050
Make sure that when you order on the app,

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:27.340
you click the no contact delivery option.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.530
Most of the big apps, Postmates,
Caviar, they all have them.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:32.220
Next, when you get the items,

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.120
make sure that when you
bring them in your home,

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.090
you wash your hands first,
then you unpack the items,

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.170
you wash your hands again, you eat,

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:40.990
and you touch some of the containers,

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:42.830
afterwards, wash your hands again.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.722
It's really about washing your hands,

00:07:44.722 --> 00:07:46.100
washing your hands,

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:46.980
washing your hands.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.266
And just know, if someone who had COVID-19

00:07:49.266 --> 00:07:52.180
handled your food, it's
a very low likelihood

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:53.650
that you will actually get the virus

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:55.170
transmitted to you through that way.

